- # `↯/s.31.1` — `Reference.Error`
+ # `↯/s.31.1` — `Reference.Error`

- Raised by Gnossienne when a reference cannot be resolved.
+ Lo lanza Gnossienne cuando no se puede resolver una referencia.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- A reference token (typically embedded in markdown or another
- structured document) could not be resolved to a target. The
- constructor takes the offending `reference` text along with a
- `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `the reference $reference
+ Un token de referencia (normalmente incrustado en Markdown o en otro documento estructurado) no
+ se pudo resolver a un destino. El constructor toma el texto `reference` problemático junto con un
+ `reason: Reason`; el mensaje representado es `the reference $reference

- could not be resolved because $reason`.
+ could not be resolved because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.31.1.1` — `NotFound`
+ ### `↯/s.31.1.1` — `NotFound`

- No target with the given reference was present in the resolver's
- store.
+ En el almacén del resolutor no había ningún destino con la referencia dada.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.31.1.1] the reference hamlet.md could not be resolved because no target with that reference was found in the store`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.31.1.1] the reference hamlet.md could not be resolved because no target with that reference was found in the store`

- **Resolution.** Confirm the target exists and the reference text
- matches it exactly (case sensitivity, anchors, etc.).
+ **Solución.** Confirma que el destino existe y que el texto de la referencia coincide con él
+ exactamente (distinción entre mayúsculas y minúsculas, anclas, etc.).

